  "prompt": "Decoding into a struct that embeds a nil pointer to an unexported struct type (type outer struct { *inner }) panics with a reflect error when the document sets a field promoted from the embedded type, either directly (Z = 1) or under a table header. It must return the error \"toml: cannot set embedded pointer to unexported struct: <package>.<type>\" (for example \"toml: cannot set embedded pointer to unexported struct: toml_test.unexportedEmbedInner\"), like encoding/json, and never panic; this applies to every decoding path, including captured raw values. A non-nil embedded pointer must keep decoding normally. Fix it.",
